    "20 April 1910"
  ],
  "explanation": "Three distinct opening dates are directly stated across the sources for what appears to be three different stations named 'Araki Station':\n\n1. **April 1, 1958** (Document D1S4): This refers to the opening of Araki Station on the Abiko Branch Line of the Narita Line.\n2. **January 1, 1960** (Document D2S4): This also refers to Araki Station on the Abiko Branch Line of the Narita Line, but conflicts with the earlier date.\n3. **20 April 1910** (Documents D3S5, D4S1, D5S2): This refers to Araki Station on the Kagoshima Main Line, operated by Japanese Government Railways (JGR).\n\nSince these are distinct stations (different lines and locations), their opening dates are valid and complementary."
}
